m look we need to get this  investigated properly yeah um what about  the suggestions that fans were pushing  their way into the ground and they  didn't have tickets that's not the sort  of behavior that the government would  condone  no it's not of course it isn't um but as  i say we need to get this properly  looked into so we understand exactly  what happened but as i say i saw uh  footage of fans behaving in a perfectly  calm way um getting pepper sprayed and  that just strikes me looking at those  pictures as not appropriate so we need  an investigation to just get to the  bottom of all of this i think uefa are  best placed to do that and i hope they  get on with it and do it urgently talk  to me about what's going on in the  papers at the weekend suggesting that  carrie johnson's organised a couple of  parties in the downing street flat now  and that and that is continuing to  rumble on should it be investigated  well i think we've had an unbelievably  comprehensive set of investigations  going on now for a period of nearly six  months we've had obviously the su grey  investigation published last week and  we've also actually interviewed i mean  goodness knows dozens or possibly even  hundreds of people in the course of her  investigation looked at emails messages  um and everything else and we've had the  metropolitan police investigation  which again has gone over and gone on  over a number of months and they  conducted that with full police powers  so having had two separate  investigations including by the police  over many months it's not immediately  obvious to me that we need  any more investigations when this has  probably been the most rightly it's  rightly been the most thoroughly  investigated um set of incidents in in  recent times but the suggestion is that  there are um whatsapp messages that put  her in the flat on the day of the prime  minister's birthday with other people in  the apartment as well messages uh that  sue gray has not seen  for completeness should we not just look  at that yeah so i saw this story saying  that um a number 10 aide had said they  had further messages and but i also um  saw the commentary that obviously sue  gray had approached and the metropolitan  police had approached everybody i think  including this aid um over the last few  months inviting them to hand over  whatever evidence they didn't want to do  that they did they didn't want to submit  it they wanted to show it to her but not  submit it they were anxious about it  coming back to them yeah and the thing i  read in the paper and i'm simply going  on what i saw in the paper i've got no  sort of special knowledge of this  suggested that offer um to that was made  available the opportunity of showing the  message rather than giving a copy and  but it wasn't followed up i'm simply  going on what i saw um in the paper as i  said i've got no um  inside knowledge of this and but my  instinctive reaction is that there have  been two incredibly thorough  investigations that have gone on um and  unless there's something really  striking that hasn't been known about  previously then then i think they have  been looked into really thoroughly and  and the report was incredibly thorough  and another one to come obviously from  um mps so we'll wait for that um talk to  me about the ministerial code um it  looks at some of the pm's uh rewritten  forward to the ministerial code removing  all reference to honesty integrity  transparency and accountability why has  it done that well i mean the nolan  principles you're referring to i think  run through  all of public life the decision to  update this code i believe was taken and  the decision to update it in this way  was taken i think about a year ago in  april 2021 all of the uh the rules about  the importance of being honest with  parliament and all of those things are  still in there  the main change which i think is  something which the um the committee on  standards in public life 