asures  pounds and ounces and the like is that  really what people care about when  they're going to be i think 800 pounds  poorer despite what the government's  offering them um  as part of this 15 billion pound package  well i think it's just allowing a bit of  a bit of our national heritage and  culture back onto the back onto the shop  shelf and you mentioned the cost of  living and of course last week the  government announced a enormous 15  billion pound package to help the cost  of living challenges that we face and in  fact for the the uh poorest one-third of  households that support package  announced last week will amount to 1  200 pounds you know really substantial  contribution and that's on top of  everything else we've had this year the  cut in fuel duty by five p elite the  national living wage  increased by a thousand pounds per year  um two million universal credit  claimants getting an extra thousand  pounds because the taper leaf taper rate  has been adjusted so the government is  is throwing everything at this cost of  living uh problem as we rightly should  and yet and yet and yet the house of  commons library says average earner will  be 800 pounds poorer despite those  support payments  well i mean i think as the chancellor  said last last week um you know we this  is a global uh cost of living challenge  it's not happening not just in the uk  it's happening in america  in france germany across the western  world caused by a whole number of things  um the  bounce back from covid supply chain  problems in china where they're still  having lockdowns  the russia ukraine crisis a whole number  of issues  are feeding this across the western  world and what we're doing in the uk  is everything possible to try and  ameliorate and soften the the blow that  these cost of living challenges are  posing what we unveiled last week  was far more than the labour party had  proposed the package this year so far  amounts to 37 billion pounds  people are  it's 